WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.326 --> 00:00:03.190
- I got myself some cool
little platform Vans.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.970
- [Interviewer] Yes, I see that,

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.388
you're three inches taller now.

00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:09.055
(Ronnie laughs)

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.490
All right, Ronnie.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.575
Ronnie, welcome back to LA.

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:17.408
- Thank you (laughing)

00:00:17.408 --> 00:00:19.730
- [Interviewer] So last
time we spoke was what?

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.410
Probably last fall, right?
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.600
- [Interviewer] That
was before Thanksgiving?

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.433
- Yes.

00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:26.057
- [Interviewer] And
what's gone on since then?

00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:26.990
'Cause you were leaving
just a couple of days

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.655
after I had spoke to you.

00:00:28.655 --> 00:00:31.750
- So what's been going on since then.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.880
I left after, the day after Thanksgiving

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.180
is when I got back to Texas.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.660
- [Interviewer] Your family is there?

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.010
- Yes, my family picked me up

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:44.623
and I was staying with a
family friend for a little bit.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.330
See, it took about...

00:00:49.365 --> 00:00:54.183
I got on methadone on December 9th,

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.983
and I've been on methadone before.

00:00:57.983 --> 00:01:01.890
It's kinda one of those
things I was on and off doing.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.940
And I got back on it

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.080
and from then I was just continuing

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.590
to try and get into rehab

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.556
and I think it was just
a little bit difficult

00:01:11.556 --> 00:01:13.412
because of the seasons.

00:01:13.412 --> 00:01:17.860
And when I called, I told
my methadone counselor

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.430
that I was trying to get into

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:20.790
this place called Nexus Recovery,

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.260
the one I had been in when I was pregnant.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:27.020
And it devastated me because they told me

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.660
that I wasn't gonna be able
to get into the program

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.260
and I just...

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.537
I remember that feeling
of just feeling like,

00:01:38.537 --> 00:01:40.950
"Damn, I'm not gonna be able to go in."

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.600
- [Interviewer] You couldn't get in why?

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.610
- Just because the last time,

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.710
the program I wanted to be in was PBWC,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:47.980
which was parenting women

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.610
and women with children
and pregnant women.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.990
And that program--

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.560
- [Interviewer] 'Cause your
son is one year old now?

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.060
- Yes, he's one years old now.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.720
The last time I had been in that program,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.100
I was nine months pregnant.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:07.990
The year before I had gotten
out, December 15th, of 2018

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:12.320
I had my son January 13th, of 2019.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.730
And when I called,

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.330
they told me that I wasn't
gonna be able to get in

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.950
for the simple fact that I
don't have custody of my child

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.690
and I'm not pregnant.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.960
And the program that they
wanted me to be in was AW,

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.520
which is adult women.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.223
And that program is two weeks.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:31.100
That's not enough time,

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.880
that is enough time for me to get healthy

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.280
and go back out on a run,

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.600
is what I look at it as.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.480
It's just ridiculous.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.633
- [Interviewer] And you've been to rehab,

00:02:38.633 --> 00:02:39.510
how many times now?

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.460
- This was gonna be my,
what was 16th, 16th or 17th.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.970
Yeah, this is my, I've lost count.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.736
I know it was either 16th or my 17th time.

00:02:48.736 --> 00:02:52.863
And goodness gracious,
so many rehabs, right?

00:02:52.863 --> 00:02:54.903
Rehabs, detoxes, all of that.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.313
Wait, hold on.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.190
What does it mean?

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.160
I'm not gonna go back
and recount all of them,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.930
whatever, the last video
was, it's one more than that.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.120
- [Interviewer] A dozen so or so.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.850
- So after that, I remember going home

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.007
from the methadone clinic and
just crying to my mom like,

00:03:15.007 --> 00:03:16.827
"They're not gonna take me,

00:03:16.827 --> 00:03:20.410
"and I really need this
program, I really need it."

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:24.193
And my mom,

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.460
I just asked her, "Will you pray with me?"

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.750
and I'm kinda not really the
most religious person ever,

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.370
but I remember asking her to pray with me

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:36.660
and we prayed right before
she dropped me back off.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.030
And the next day when she went

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:43.770
to help to pick me up to
go back to the clinic,

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:47.527
she was telling me,

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:50.260
not to be too down about it,
that there's just other rehabs,

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.000
just give it a second,
just give some time.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.410
And I remember when I went to
the methadone clinic that day,

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.947
my counselor told me, "Hey, all right,

00:03:57.947 --> 00:03:59.830
"are you gonna be ready December 23rd?"

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.340
And I said, "December 23rd, for what?"

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.820
And he said, "They're gonna
admit you to the PBWC program".

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:08.970
So I ended up getting the program I wanted

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.400
and I ended up committing the first day

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.230
to do the 90 days instead of just the 30.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.653
And when I got there,

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.003
I remember,

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.860
it was kind of a little
struggle getting admitted

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.620
and I started to get
really anxious about it

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.720
and I was having like really bad anxiety.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.010
I was gonna have a panic,

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.088
I felt like I was gonna
have a panic attack

00:04:38.088 --> 00:04:38.921
on the way over there.

00:04:39.822 --> 00:04:40.903
In the car, it was just me and my dad.

00:04:42.039 --> 00:04:44.120
And I was just like (humming)

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.870
I just felt like the
tightness in my chest,

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.890
it was just so, it hurt almost.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.140
- [Interviewer] And what
was that anxiety about?

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.080
- Just going to rehab.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.020
- [Interviewer] I mean just
how difficult it was gonna be

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.450
to stop heroin?

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:59.340
- Yeah, it was the thought of
like, "I know I can do this."

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.160
I've been off heroin before,

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.440
I've been clean.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.750
I know it was only only six months,

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:09.410
but to me that was a lot,
because I've never tried before.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.510
And I just, I knew I could do it.

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:13.913
I knew I had it in me,

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.293
but I was afraid that I was gonna fail.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:24.173
So after I got dropped
off, that was on the 23rd.

00:05:27.535 --> 00:05:29.630
The next few weeks of me being

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.948
in rehab was really difficult for me

00:05:31.948 --> 00:05:36.948
because I think I had
been too hard on myself,

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.463
I was just like,

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.003
I was so terrified of messing up again

00:05:43.003 --> 00:05:47.160
and relapsing that I wasn't giving myself

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.214
the opportunity to really try, to excel,

00:05:51.214 --> 00:05:55.270
to ask for help, to be happy.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:06:00.270
So, I spent a lot of
my time in rehab alone

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.423
in my room crying.

00:06:05.035 --> 00:06:09.573
I was at a point where I just felt so low.

00:06:12.172 --> 00:06:16.890
I felt like I had no strength
to get myself back up.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.410
Or maybe it was just the fact

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.303
that I didn't wanna get back up.

00:06:23.611 --> 00:06:26.366
Do you remember me telling
you in the last video

00:06:26.366 --> 00:06:28.010
about the kidnapping?

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:31.910
And I had been struggling really hard

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.573
with PTSD at this point.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.740
And I'm talking like
there's a specific pair

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:41.470
of flip flops that I would see,

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:45.460
that this girl had and it
was the exact same flip flops

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.700
that I had wore here,

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.480
when I had first became homeless
and they had picked me up

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.140
and took me to the hotel.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.913
It was that same pair of sandals.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.253
I went haywire.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.940
My brain went into that
fight or flight mode,

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.630
like, "I have to get out of here,

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.530
"I have to get out of here,
I have to get out of here."

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.327
Like, "They're coming, someone's watching,

00:07:05.327 --> 00:07:06.790
"they're gonna get me."

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.300
And this is a 100% sober,

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.070
'cause of course I'm in rehab

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:16.070
and I was constantly
checking the shower curtains

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:19.420
to see if somebody was behind them,

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.713
checking under my bed
before I went to sleep.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:26.620
I would go as far as
looking down the crack

00:07:27.711 --> 00:07:30.530
between the wall and my
mattress at nighttime,

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.403
because of how afraid I was.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:39.240
And that was costing a
lot of energy for me.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:42.280
It was draining me completely.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:46.845
And that went on for the
whole time I was in rehab.

00:07:46.845 --> 00:07:51.845
Unsurprisingly, I was
being bullied at rehab.

00:07:52.644 --> 00:07:57.644
I'm a 22 year old being bullied
by 30 and 40 year old women.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:03.640
And it hurt because it
was my first day of rehab,

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:07.470
the first day I got there,
everybody was just hating on me.

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.557
Nobody wanted to talk to me

00:08:09.557 --> 00:08:12.790
and I was tryna talk to
people and it didn't work out.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:15.563
People were just constantly hating on me,

00:08:15.563 --> 00:08:17.503
I could hear them talking about me,

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.810
like you don't even know me,

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:24.100
I've been here for for a
couple of weeks now, two weeks,

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.210
you've never once to talk to me.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.387
You don't even know my name.

00:08:27.387 --> 00:08:29.380
My first, my middle,

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.690
my first name, my middle
name or my last name,

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.970
but you hate me so much and I'm just,

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:38.473
I'm nasty, I'm disgusting,
I'm a whore because...

00:08:38.473 --> 00:08:39.870
What?

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.840
Because the guy that you
think is super-duper hot

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.339
that is in narcotics anonymous

00:08:44.339 --> 00:08:46.240
says hello to me every single day

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:49.770
because I know them from the
previous years I was here.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.670
And it was just little things like that,

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.410
that they just hated on me for.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:56.250
So, I had no friends in rehab.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.810
And I think that also fueled my PTSD,

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.130
with everybody knowing each other

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:06.200
and me not knowing any of them,

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.900
I felt like they were
just coming against me.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:12.123
And like I said,

00:09:12.123 --> 00:09:15.180
I got and have been into
rehab the 23rd of December

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.180
and I was kicked out of rehab

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.310
on the 7th of January, I believe,

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:24.350
no, it was the 21st,

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:27.030
I was there like, not even a month,

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:28.593
a little less than a month.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.176
I was kicked out of rehab.

00:09:32.176 --> 00:09:34.053
I remember like,

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:39.830
I was just bawling my eyes out

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:43.723
because what had happened was

00:09:43.723 --> 00:09:46.910
this girl, these two women,

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:49.260
they were like 40 years old,

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:53.110
they've got children
and they had cliqued up

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.380
and one day one of the girls,

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:59.337
it was midnight and she woke up

00:09:59.337 --> 00:10:01.460
and she wanted to get a snack

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.970
and the tech was like, "Cool,
just come to the closet."

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.980
So I decided, "Oh cool, can
I have a snack as well."

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:10.470
So I went in there and I got some Oreos

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:14.520
and the very next
morning, which was Sunday,

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.220
that same girl that we had
gotten cookies together

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.437
at the same time, looked at me and said,

00:10:20.437 --> 00:10:22.587
"Don't ever try and get...

00:10:22.587 --> 00:10:25.447
"don't ever try and mess
up what I got going on

00:10:25.447 --> 00:10:27.640
"when I'm going to get snacks".

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.927
And I looked at her and I said,

00:10:29.927 --> 00:10:32.777
"We're all allowed to get snacks,

00:10:32.777 --> 00:10:35.007
"it's not like I took what you wanted,

00:10:35.007 --> 00:10:36.960
"you went in front of me"

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.440
and the way, she did
it, she tried to do it

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.803
in front of everybody.

00:10:40.803 --> 00:10:43.470
It's Sunday morning, we're
all getting ready for church

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:44.440
and we're in the butt hut,

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:47.230
which is where we have
to smoke our cigarettes.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:50.939
And she says it in front of everybody.

00:10:50.939 --> 00:10:53.977
And I look at her and I tried
to be respectful and say,

00:10:53.977 --> 00:10:56.347
"Well, anybody can get cookies,

00:10:56.347 --> 00:11:00.067
"it's not, Miss Lisa, which
was the tech is really cool.

00:11:00.067 --> 00:11:02.240
"You should not bothered by that."

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.370
And what did she say?

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:07.223
The girl looked at me and she said,

00:11:08.187 --> 00:11:10.170
"I told you not to do it."

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.457
And I looked at her and I said,

00:11:11.457 --> 00:11:13.250
"I'm allowed to get
snacks when I want to."

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.707
I said, "You're not gonna sit here

00:11:14.707 --> 00:11:17.207
"and bully me over some Oreos."

00:11:20.508 --> 00:11:23.760
Everybody was just kinda looking around,

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:27.210
I guess she thought that I
wasn't gonna stand up for myself.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:30.467
And she was just yelling like,

00:11:30.467 --> 00:11:32.997
"I'm not trying to be
disrespectful to you,

00:11:32.997 --> 00:11:36.217
"but when I tell you
something, you better listen

00:11:36.217 --> 00:11:38.297
"because," I guess she
tried to, what'd she say?

00:11:38.297 --> 00:11:41.690
"You better listen because I'm
old enough to be your mama".

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:45.037
And I looked at her and I
said, "Well, you're not my mama

00:11:45.037 --> 00:11:47.176
"and you're not gonna tell me what to do".

00:11:47.176 --> 00:11:49.450
And she made this ugly face at me,

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:50.400
She was like (grumbling)

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.273
so I just looked at her and
I went (grumbling) back,

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.023
just not good,

00:11:55.023 --> 00:11:57.584
because that type of stuff
is not my nature either,

00:11:57.584 --> 00:12:02.240
but when you're gonna sit here
and just try and pasture me,

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.850
and that wasn't the only
time she had done it.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.900
Her and her little friend had tried

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.840
to do it multiple times
over, just anything,

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:14.537
anything, I couldn't even
sneeze, if she sneezed before me,

00:12:14.537 --> 00:12:17.420
like I couldn't speak in class

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:20.190
without them trying to make some noise

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:22.583
and make me feel like I was less then,

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:26.053
I remember in class I said,

00:12:26.053 --> 00:12:28.670
"Oh, I used to not believe in Jesus".

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:29.636
And she said,

00:12:29.636 --> 00:12:30.657
(snickering)

00:12:30.657 --> 00:12:32.340
"Oh my God", like her,

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:34.090
they were both snickering and stuff.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:36.610
And I was just like, "what?"

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.053
So this had been on for the whole time

00:12:38.053 --> 00:12:39.700
that I was there in rehab.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.959
And the reason I got
kicked out was because,

00:12:41.959 --> 00:12:44.573
one of the girls,

00:12:44.573 --> 00:12:47.480
we were in a narcotics anonymous meeting

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:51.040
and you're only allowed to
sit in the first five rows

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:55.370
and there's 31 girls and five rows.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:13:00.370
So, I set three rows and four seats over

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:03.290
from one of those girls,
one of the mean ones.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:07.640
And she says, "I can't see.",

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.750
and I don't know who she's talking to,

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:13.580
so I just keep on, and she was
like, "Hello, I can't see".

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.540
And I'm sitting, I turned around,

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.840
and she's all the way back
there, I'm all the way up here.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.620
She's on the fifth row, I'm on the third.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:21.587
I'm on the...

00:13:21.587 --> 00:13:22.810
Yeah, I'm on the second

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:24.620
'cause I sat three in front of her.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:29.620
And she started yelling and
she got up, got in my face,

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:32.947
started cursing at me specifically said,

00:13:32.947 --> 00:13:34.980
"You're not gonna be here long".

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.600
Walked up, got her baby and left.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.699
And then the program director, he's...

00:13:40.699 --> 00:13:43.560
Like when we're in the
auditorium, there's two doors.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:45.930
His office is right on the other side

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:48.570
of this left-hand door.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:53.510
And I hear her crying,
saying that I'm bullying her

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:58.025
and I'm being mean to
her, and within two hours

00:13:58.025 --> 00:14:03.025
after that happening, he
pulls me aside and he says,

00:14:03.417 --> 00:14:05.730
"You need to pack your belongings."

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:09.440
And they were gonna drop
me off on a street corner

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.743
with all of my stuff.

00:14:11.878 --> 00:14:13.867
They said, "We can't do anything for you,

00:14:13.867 --> 00:14:15.400
"we can't help you get..."

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:16.727
And I said, "Well, if
you're gonna kick me out,

00:14:16.727 --> 00:14:18.767
"you can't give me like a
couple of days to figure out

00:14:18.767 --> 00:14:20.605
"where to live?"

00:14:20.605 --> 00:14:23.560
I was supposed to live at
this rehab for 90 days,

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:24.833
I made it 21.

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:31.200
It was unfair because
he did no investigating,

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.820
no talking to other people in class

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.180
to see what had really happened,

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.480
'cause if he would've, he would've known

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:41.000
that everybody saw that she
got up and got in my face,

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.080
but I was a problem.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:45.590
So I ended up getting kicked out

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:49.530
and I called my mom and
she was really upset

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:52.880
because she thought that
I had done something

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.237
and I told her, "Mom,
I didn't do anything.

00:14:55.237 --> 00:14:56.410
"They are bullying me."

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:57.830
And my mom had known

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.890
when I had been in that exact same rehab

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:03.109
when I was pregnant, I
was bullied a lot as well.

00:15:03.109 --> 00:15:06.845
I get bullied a lot of places that I go,

00:15:06.845 --> 00:15:09.270
out here on the streets.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.190
You wouldn't imagine how bad I get it.

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:13.750
I can walk by a female's tent,

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:15.660
a female in her boyfriend's tent

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.020
to go to that store
right there to get a soda

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:21.119
and walk back in that same
direction right in front of her,

00:15:21.119 --> 00:15:24.050
and the she will straight
up get out of her tent

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:25.210
and start yelling at me and tell me,

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.660
she's gonna beat me up if
I don't get moving along.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.819
And I'm looking at her like,
"I don't know who you are.

00:15:29.819 --> 00:15:31.587
"I don't, who are you?

00:15:31.587 --> 00:15:33.940
"I'm going to get a drink."

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.120
- [Interviewer] It's good that
you stand up for yourself.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:38.230
- Yeah, and I'm just like,
it's just ridiculous the way

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:39.765
that people act sometimes.

00:15:39.765 --> 00:15:44.765
And, so I remember when my mom was like,

00:15:45.857 --> 00:15:47.607
"That makes no sense, why wouldn't he talk

00:15:47.607 --> 00:15:48.817
"to other people in class?

00:15:48.817 --> 00:15:50.890
"Why wouldn't he do
this and this and that?"

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:51.917
And I said, "Mama, you know what?

00:15:51.917 --> 00:15:53.130
"I don't know".

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:54.840
When I really thought about
it, I think the reason

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.520
why they kicked me out instead of her

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.470
was because she had her
newborn child with her.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.680
But that's still unfair.

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:03.150
I should not have gotten
kicked out like that.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.750
They should have found her
another program to go to.

00:16:07.851 --> 00:16:10.174
So anyways, I ended up getting picked up

00:16:10.174 --> 00:16:12.093
and I had nowhere to go.

00:16:14.857 --> 00:16:17.450
My mom and dad picked me
up and my son was at home

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:20.010
with my grandpa and grandma

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.620
and they ended up...

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.450
I was so scared because,

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:28.623
I didn't think I was ready.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.577
I felt like, "How am I?

00:16:33.577 --> 00:16:36.396
"How can I possibly stay clean now?

00:16:36.396 --> 00:16:40.245
Here I am, super upset.

00:16:40.245 --> 00:16:45.140
I'm having constant PTSD
episodes every other day.

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:48.330
I can't sleep at night because
I'm waking up screaming,

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:50.046
I'm having nightmares.

00:16:50.046 --> 00:16:54.560
I had no clue what to do.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:58.957
It was just, I honestly thought,

00:16:58.957 --> 00:17:01.157
"You're not gonna make it, Ronnie.

00:17:01.157 --> 00:17:02.117
"You're not gonna make it.

00:17:02.117 --> 00:17:04.787
"Just give up, this is it.

00:17:04.787 --> 00:17:08.557
"You tried, oh well, at
least we tried Ronnie,

00:17:08.557 --> 00:17:12.320
"you can just keep walking
along, who cares now?"

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.710
And I remember when I got in the car

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:18.987
and I told my mom and dad
and I said, "I'm scared."

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:24.800
And they were like, "what do you mean?"

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:29.800
And I said, "I don't know
if I'm gonna make it."

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.963
And the place I was gonna go was,

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:40.810
one of my friends and he
was a very good friend,

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.380
we've been friends since high school

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:47.380
and him and I had both gone
through addiction together

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:52.040
and he was clean now and
he owns his apartment

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:54.403
and he had a job, he was doing good.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:59.090
Now, the problem with staying there was,

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:02.130
it was about a 20 minute walk

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:05.460
from the apartment to my drug dealer

00:18:10.674 --> 00:18:14.250
This is like the worst position
I could put myself into.

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.103
That's like me asking to just

00:18:16.103 --> 00:18:18.542
be tormented every single day

00:18:18.542 --> 00:18:20.617
that I wake up.

00:18:20.617 --> 00:18:25.617
And I just told my mom, I
said, "I can't go there, mom.

00:18:26.617 --> 00:18:28.627
"I can't go there", and she said,

00:18:28.627 --> 00:18:29.917
"What do you mean you can't go there?

00:18:29.917 --> 00:18:31.547
"I thought you said it was a good place,

00:18:31.547 --> 00:18:32.757
"I thought you said he was clean,

00:18:32.757 --> 00:18:34.717
"I thought you said he was...

00:18:34.717 --> 00:18:37.080
"Everything was good,
there was no drugs there".

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.447
And I said, "Yeah, there's no drugs there,

00:18:38.447 --> 00:18:40.920
"but there's drugs 20
minutes down the street".

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:45.010
And she ended up making
some phone calls and finding

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.600
a friend that I could stay with again

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.013
until I got into rehab.

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:58.923
And I ended up doing that.

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:05.680
And, I've steady waiting on
court, steady waiting on court

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:10.200
for my CPS so that I can go to,

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.770
I can get my son back

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:14.910
and I can live back at
home with my parents

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:18.053
till I can start working
and get on my feet again.

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:27.290
So I spent every single
day at that rehab at Nexus,

00:19:27.670 --> 00:19:31.690
they have a program called
the recovery resources

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.490
and you're allowed to go
up to Nexus and hang out

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:36.350
with them every single day,

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:38.050
all day if you want to.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.780
And that's what I did.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:44.240
I got on five different buses and trains

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:47.966
to get from Granbury to Dallas,

00:19:47.966 --> 00:19:51.800
to hang out at this
recovery resource center

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.680
just to stay clean.

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:56.230
And everybody was like, why do
you come all the way up here?

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:59.870
It's a two hour drive.

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:04.209
So, imagine having to get
picked up by my father

00:20:04.209 --> 00:20:09.020
on his way to work 'cause he
worked in Downtown Fort Worth,

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:12.040
pick me up, drive all the
way to Downtown Fort Worth.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:15.720
Then me having to walk two miles

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:18.585
to get to the train
station, hop on the train,

00:20:18.585 --> 00:20:22.430
go all the way to Dallas,
get off of that train,

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:25.530
walk a little bit to go
onto the other train,

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:27.380
get on that train, go walk a little bit

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:30.990
to get to the bus stop
to go to go all the way

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:33.580
to another bus stop and then
get picked up by another bus

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:38.190
to finally get dropped
off a couple blocks down

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:39.550
in the mean time having to walk

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.150
from that last bus stop
all the way to Nexus

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.143
just to stay clean.

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:48.727
And the thing is, they say,

00:20:48.727 --> 00:20:52.977
"If you can go through all
of these things to get dope,

00:20:52.977 --> 00:20:57.000
"you can go through all of
these things to stay clean."

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.500
And that's what I did.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:03.270
I did that daily, every single day.

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:06.660
And the recovery resources, coaches,

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:10.270
they ended up giving me a bus
pass, so I didn't have to pay

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:11.720
to be able to come up here,

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.180
'cause it was hard for me
to have to pay the bus fare

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:18.720
and the train fare and
then when I'm hungry,

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:21.060
try and find something to eat.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:23.720
So they ended up getting
me a little regional fare,

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:26.430
which is buses and trains and other,

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.273
I don't remember what the other one was.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:32.233
And I did that for quite some time.

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:36.750
Now in between that, I am not gonna lie.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:40.610
I definitely had some weak moments.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:45.070
And I had relapsed one day

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:46.477
and I called my mom and I said,

00:21:46.477 --> 00:21:49.740
"I need you to come get me, I relapsed."

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:53.960
And she came and got me
and they took me back

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:55.503
to the family friends.

00:21:55.503 --> 00:21:57.637
And 'cause at this point

00:21:57.637 --> 00:21:59.400
I'm still not allowed to live there,

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:04.400
but I finally, finally,
finally got visitation rights.

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:07.247
And I remember when my
lawyer told me like,

00:22:07.247 --> 00:22:08.790
"Yeah, you can see your son now."

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:10.922
I'm like, (cheering)

00:22:10.922 --> 00:22:13.719
I was so just, "Oh man,

00:22:13.719 --> 00:22:18.197
"I missed my son so much."

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:25.640
I definitely believe he is the only reason

00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:27.690
that I'm still alive.

00:22:27.690 --> 00:22:29.923
If I didn't have him,

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:32.890
I don't think I'd have a reason.

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:42.823
My self esteem,

00:22:44.240 --> 00:22:47.963
it has its days now where
it's getting a lot better.

00:22:50.488 --> 00:22:55.488
But I have those days where
I struggle with my PTSD

00:22:56.940 --> 00:23:01.472
and my bipolar and it's just...

00:23:01.472 --> 00:23:04.168
It got to a point where I
didn't remember (mumbles),

00:23:04.168 --> 00:23:08.261
I didn't remember when
the last time I showered,

00:23:08.261 --> 00:23:10.485
because I have been
wearing the same clothes

00:23:10.485 --> 00:23:13.181
for three, four or five days,

00:23:13.181 --> 00:23:15.550
which is gross.

00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:20.104
But that is what my depression looks like.

00:23:20.104 --> 00:23:24.240
It can take a hold of me
and that grip that it has

00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:28.610
is so tight that I'm
just, I feel restricted,

00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:32.183
I'm stuck and I have no,

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:36.210
I have no willpower to move.

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:39.690
I mean, the only reason I was breathing

00:23:39.690 --> 00:23:44.190
is just because I have to, my
body just does it by itself.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:48.120
If I actually had to
physically like do something

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:50.330
for me to breathe, I wouldn't do it.

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:51.730
Yeah, I would have given up.

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:04.000
I think that when the video came out,

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.693
I had no clue that it had even been out.

00:24:07.765 --> 00:24:09.120
I had thought about it,

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:12.070
but I never knew what your
channel was or anything.

00:24:12.070 --> 00:24:17.000
And that was the day that it happened.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:18.400
When was it?

00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:21.510
See, I think it was Jan, no,

00:24:21.510 --> 00:24:24.802
I think I found out in February.

00:24:24.802 --> 00:24:29.287
And that is when my mom
texted me and she said,

00:24:29.287 --> 00:24:31.180
"Are you ready?"

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:33.159
And I'm like, "Ready?

00:24:33.159 --> 00:24:34.530
"For what?"

00:24:34.530 --> 00:24:39.530
And she says, "Your YouTube
interview is trending".

00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:43.487
And I said, "No, it's not shut up.

00:24:43.487 --> 00:24:45.920
"Whatever, what do you
really need to tell me?"

00:24:45.920 --> 00:24:50.630
And she sends me the screenshot
of all of these people

00:24:50.630 --> 00:24:52.320
that have been sending it to her

00:24:52.320 --> 00:24:53.890
'cause she had no idea either.

00:24:53.890 --> 00:24:56.370
And all these people were like,

00:24:56.370 --> 00:24:59.350
I can get on Facebook and there's my face,

00:24:59.350 --> 00:25:01.760
she'd get on Facebook, oh there's my face,

00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:05.794
there's my face again, scrolls
up, there's my face again.

00:25:05.794 --> 00:25:10.560
And it was like everybody
that I knew had seen it.

00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:13.793
Everybody that knew my mom had seen it.

00:25:16.320 --> 00:25:20.740
I remember looking at the title

00:25:22.160 --> 00:25:24.920
and it's saying heroin addict.

00:25:24.920 --> 00:25:29.920
And I was like, "Oh, Oh." (laughing)

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:33.400
I was like, "Wow, that's
a big sucker punch."

00:25:33.400 --> 00:25:37.230
But in the beginning it
was crazy because I just,

00:25:37.230 --> 00:25:41.540
I thought like the worst,

00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:44.920
the absolute worst, that
little voice in my head

00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:47.690
that constantly tells
me that I'm not enough,

00:25:47.690 --> 00:25:51.060
that people are judging me went haywire.

00:25:51.060 --> 00:25:52.960
My thoughts were just like,

00:25:52.960 --> 00:25:54.769
I thought it was over, it's done.

00:25:54.769 --> 00:25:58.240
Everybody's gonna judge me,
everybody's gonna hate me.

00:25:58.240 --> 00:26:00.930
Everybody's gonna have
something to say about me.

00:26:00.930 --> 00:26:05.930
And all this negativity
just flooded my entire...

00:26:07.360 --> 00:26:09.223
My entire being,

00:26:10.210 --> 00:26:13.510
it was filled with nothing but negative,

00:26:13.510 --> 00:26:16.060
negative, negative, negative.

00:26:16.060 --> 00:26:18.840
And I hadn't even watched the video,

00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:21.740
I hadn't even taken the time,

00:26:21.740 --> 00:26:24.730
just no, nothing because my...

00:26:26.730 --> 00:26:28.603
I was scared.

00:26:31.110 --> 00:26:36.110
There was not one positive
thought in my head, not one.

00:26:37.114 --> 00:26:41.877
It's like, "How can that even be,

00:26:47.077 --> 00:26:52.077
"how is it that there's
not a single good thing

00:26:53.277 --> 00:26:56.113
"that I can think or say about myself?

00:26:58.037 --> 00:27:03.037
"How is it that, I spend
so much time trying

00:27:06.467 --> 00:27:11.467
"to do positive affirmations
and tell myself I love myself

00:27:12.127 --> 00:27:13.490
"and tell myself I'm beautiful."

00:27:13.490 --> 00:27:17.413
But when I saw all those views

00:27:20.410 --> 00:27:23.310
and all those people who were
texting me and messaging me.

00:27:28.758 --> 00:27:33.253
I couldn't even comprehend anything.

00:27:35.224 --> 00:27:40.224
I ended up not going home for three days,

00:27:40.610 --> 00:27:43.290
I didn't talk to anybody for three days,

00:27:43.290 --> 00:27:48.290
I didn't respond to anybody, nothing.

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:53.615
I didn't open any messages,
any videos, anything

00:27:53.615 --> 00:27:55.603
No calls, nothing.

00:27:57.910 --> 00:28:02.910
And the one person that
did help me through

00:28:06.700 --> 00:28:09.700
is my friend Chris.

00:28:09.700 --> 00:28:14.700
And he had been locked up for
a little over a year or so.

00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:25.780
And I hadn't talked to him forever.

00:28:25.780 --> 00:28:29.567
So when he was finally out,
I asked him, "Hey, will you

00:28:29.567 --> 00:28:33.567
"watch this video and
tell me what you think."

00:28:35.730 --> 00:28:38.643
And I said, "I need help
getting through this".

00:28:40.370 --> 00:28:45.327
And he did, he watched the
whole video and he said,

00:28:45.327 --> 00:28:49.450
"Ronnie, there's nothing bad in there".

00:28:49.450 --> 00:28:52.367
He said, "There nothing wrong with it".

